    "initialOwnerSequence": "Locked SourceLoginViewModel initializes getHeaderMap(true), then getStoredLoginInfoMap(). It does not derive defaults through getLoginInfoMap(). Missing or non-Map raw data yields an empty working map; unreadable native owner still throws STATE_IO.",
    "renderSequence": [
      "Static loginUi parses through original RowUi/GSON. Dynamic getLoginUiJs prepends getLoginJs() and normalizes the actual Rhino completion through retained normalizeRuleJsResult before the same GSON parser.",
      "evalUiJsResult binds java/source/sourceApi to the original source, a copy of the current real Java Map as result, null Book/Chapter for this standalone sheet, and the existing source library/environment. It does not call login() or the form-action Java host.",
      "Each nonliteral viewName expression separately prepends the login script. It receives the actual working map overlaid only by displayed text/password edits/defaults. The dynamic form body is not rerun or retained as a new VM for labels.",
      "A quoted viewName of UTF-16 length3...19 is a literal. Normal label evaluation failures flow through evalUiJsResult.getOrNull into the old row builder null-label branch; cancellation/control failures propagate.",
      "Selector/toggle construction initializes only the transient dialog map using the locked nil-chars placeholders/defaults. Explicit empty arrays remain distinct. No generated credential defaults are stored merely to render.",
      "The locked legacy rowUiBuilder has only text/password/select/button/toggle cases and no label/unknown branch. Raw original rows/types remain in the transport DTO, while their omitted UI nodes are skipped without executing their labels, inventing inputs or rejecting an otherwise valid form.",
      "Old render jobs are cancelled; resolveLoginUiRender applies successful rows and preserves prior valid rows on failure. Confirmation requires non-null successfully rendered rowUis, including a valid empty array."
    ]
  },
  "production": [
    "Product BookSourceFormLoginView.loadUI classifies off main. Traditional sources use the existing BookSourceFetcher.mainJSService, its same source actor lock/revision/NativeLegadoOriginalPreviewExecutor/LegadoRuntimeProcess and ordinary original JVM/Rhino. Nontraditional loadLegacyUI retains its prior route; no JSC fallback is added for traditional rendering.",
    "New OriginalLoginUIRuntime delegates original source/header/raw credential/cache/Cookie operations to the same RuleEnvironment/RuntimeTask/Host owners. RuleModels exposes its existing stored-Map helper internally, avoiding a second parser or credential store.",
    "Package loginUIOriginal and typed RowUi/style/labels/values DTOs use existing executeOriginal task/deadline/cancel/effects transport. The App projects those canonical typed rows directly into existing LoginField/style/Grid without invoking LoginManager lenient JSC normalization.",
    "Original selectors retain every declared choice including empty strings, never append undeclared stored choices, and use the locked Spinner.setSelectionSafely clamped display index without changing the working map. Original toggles keep all choices and their initialized working value, with no two-state restriction or empty-string fallback. Original adapter positions provide stable choice IDs even for repeated labels. Legacy/TTS rules are unchanged.",
    "Original raw label/unknown nodes are omitted, and positional original row IDs preserve distinct duplicate-name controls/labels. Nil select/toggle options project their locked placeholders; original selectors with explicit empty options stay selection controls, rather than becoming editable text fields. Other existing source/TTS empty-options behavior is unchanged.",
